Security decisions and rationale
- I intentionally did NOT add any plaintext prints of passwords or recovery codes to repository code (this is insecure and risks secret leakage). Instead I
added a safe debug flag that logs masked prefixes only.
- Recommendations for production hardening (not yet implemented here):
  - Use a password-specific hash (Argon2, bcrypt, or scrypt) rather than raw SHA-256 for user password storage and verification.
  - Treat recovery tokens as single-use, store only token hashes, and set short expirations.
  - Add rate-limiting and monitoring for recovery attempts.
  - Ensure logs never contain full secrets and redact any sensitive values.

